In article <1992Feb3.200914.4164@leland.Stanford.EDU>, jrawles@leland.Stanford.EDU (jody rawles) writes...
> The manual (Net Hack 3.0) refers to metacharacter as in -
>	"Keyboards that have a meta key can also use these extended commands"
> 
> I want to use these extended commands, but I don't know which key is the
> meta key on a mac? a Sun Sparc? a vt100?  could someone please post or mail
> the answer.
> 
> Or, am I wrong.  Is there any other way to jump, loot, offer, pray, etc.?

     Type '#', followed by the name of the extended command, followed by
<return> (or <enter>, or whatever it's called on your keyboard).  Depending
on compilation settings, you may only need the first letter of the command
instead of the whole word.  That title is a bit misleading; the reason those
commands are classed as "extended" is because there just aren't enough keys
to go around.  If you turn on number_pad mode, some of those other commands
are activated by the letter keys usually reserved for movement.

